     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Thanks for searching around, Brandon. I guess I will try and compress the files on my PC at work and see if that works. <div>I just wanted to reduce file size for uploading figures to a journal. They are pretty large as is. Cheers. <br><br>On Monday, April 6, 2015 at 10:53:02 AM UTC-4, Brandon Hurr wrote:<div><div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Mon, Apr 6, 2015 at 6:25 AM, wade ross <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">cwad...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">width </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">8.5</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> height </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">5</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> units </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&quot;in&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> pointsize </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">12</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> res</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">1000</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> compression</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&quot;lzw&quot;</span></blockquote></div><br></div><div>Sorry Wade, last week was busy so I could only guess. After further google-fu you aren&#39;t the first to try this and have difficulty. </div><div><br></div><div>I did find this: </div><div><a href=\"http://stackoverflow.com/questions/17218305/tiff-resolution-and-compression-are-not-reliably-set-in-osx\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://stackoverflow.com/questions/17218305/tiff-resolution-and-compression-are-not-reliably-set-in-osx&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792369288572000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1Z4fLjKN6yrAnYVYIrldmP\">http://stackoverflow.com/<u></u>questions/17218305/tiff-<u></u>resolution-and-compression-<u></u>are-not-reliably-set-in-osx</a><br></div><div><br></div><div>I&#39;m on a mac so this makes sense for me: </div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\" size=\"1\">#creation of dataset and plot</font></div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\" size=\"1\">df&lt;-data.frame(x=1:10, y=1:10)<br>ggplot(data=df, aes(x=x, y=y))+geom_point()<br>#170 MB file<br>ggsave(&quot;compressed.not.tiff&quot;, plot = last_plot(), width = 8.5, height = 5, units = &quot;in&quot;, pointsize = 12, dpi=1000)<br># 443 kB file<br>ggsave(&quot;compressed.is.tiff&quot;, plot = last_plot(), width = 8.5, height = 5, units = &quot;in&quot;, pointsize = 12, dpi=1000, compression=&quot;lzw&quot;, type=&quot;cairo&quot;)</font><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\" size=\"1\"><br></font></div>I don&#39;t have a windows or Linux machine so I&#39;m unsure how useful this will be for you. <div><br></div><div>B</div></div>\r\n</blockquote></div></div></div></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p></blockquote></div></div>"
