   "subject": "Re: Compression options in ggplot2",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">The journal recommends .tiff for reasons unknown. <br>For now, I will use the following code which SUBSTANTIALLY reduces file size: (note: it does not use the ggsave function)<div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">tiff</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">filename </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;yourfilepathandfilename.tiff&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> width </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">8.5</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> height </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">5</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> units </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;in&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> pointsize </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">12</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> res</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1000</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> compression</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;lzw&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>ggplot</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(...)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># This is the ggplot figure code</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>dev</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">off</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># This closes the tiff device after drawing the figure </span></div></code></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"color:rgb(11,83,148);font-family:verdana,sans-serif;font-size:12.8000001907349px\"><br></div><br>On Monday, April 6, 2015 at 11:12:39 AM UTC-4, Brandon Hurr wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">If that is the case I remember seeing someone on StackOverflow suggesting saving as a PDF (vector based, so the files would be very small too). Try that as well and compare the results. <div><br></div><div>Also, there is this which suggests eps as well. </div><div><a href=\"http://thepoliticalmethodologist.com/2013/11/25/making-high-resolution-graphics-for-academic-publishing/\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://thepoliticalmethodologist.com/2013/11/25/making-high-resolution-graphics-for-academic-publishing/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792369288575000&amp;usg=AOvVaw06w2QMe8qokUM21ypZLExf\">http://thepoliticalmethodologist.com/2013/11/25/making-high-resolution-graphics-for-academic-publishing/</a><br></div></div><div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Mon, Apr 6, 2015 at 8:09 AM, wade ross <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">cwad...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Thanks for searching around, Brandon. I guess I will try and compress the files on my PC at work and see if that works. <div>I just wanted to reduce file size for uploading figures to a journal. They are pretty large as is. Cheers. <br><br>On Monday, April 6, 2015 at 10:53:02 AM UTC-4, Brandon Hurr wrote:<div><div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Mon, Apr 6, 2015 at 6:25 AM, wade ross <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a rel=\"nofol